From 781fb8995f79ca9f37a85d8adcd717c7b3ebbb6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:37:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Available-skills dimming confusion, PixelBot-only avatars, chat pfps, brand color

Dashboard home cards: the "Available skills" strip dimmed by enabled
state, but only Showtime's badge component actually supports a dim/
color distinction — Reputation Manager's and Cold Open's don't (no
enabled prop on those two), so a freshly-installed, unconfigured
workspace showed Showtime's skills grayed to near-invisible while the
other product's stayed full-color, reading as "only some skills are
even available" when they all equally were. Available no longer dims
by enabled state at all — that's what the separate Enabled row is for.

Avatars: dropped Micah and Open Peeps per direct request — just
PixelBot now, with the category-tabs UI (pointless for one option)
removed from the picker along with the now-dead category state.
Added a transparentBackground option to the shared generator (no
background rect at all, for a surface that already has its own), and
wired real chat avatars into TeammatesChat — the user's own real
avatar next to their messages, a fixed PixelBot seed representing
"the worker" next to its replies, both small (16px) and transparent so
they sit on the message row instead of looking like a filled badge.
Fetched via a new GET /api/user/avatar (TeammatesChat is instantiated
from three separate trees with no single server-component ancestor to
thread a prop through).

Library: the "Installed" badge was emerald green, inconsistent with
the amber brand color used everywhere else this session — matched it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
